{"schemaVersion":1,"canonicalId":"eu-ft:topic:JUST-2019-AG-DRUGS","identifier":"JUST-2019-AG-DRUGS","sourceReference":"31115548HOMEActionGrant1569369600000","source":"EU Funding & Tenders Portal","sourceType":"1","mechanism":"grant","title":"Supporting Initiatives in the Field of Drugs Policy","callIdentifier":"JUST-2019-AG-DRUGS","programmeCode":"31070247","programmePeriod":"2014 - 2020","status":"closed","sourceStatusCodes":["31094503"],"openings":["2019-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"],"deadlines":["2020-01-29T17:00:00.000Z"],"nextDeadline":null,"deadlineModel":"single-stage","description":"Scope : The aim of this call is to contribute to the effective and coherent application of EU law and to support development of new approaches in the area of drugs. The priorities are: - to support activities in the area of epidemiology of use of new psychoactive substances, including potent synthetic opioids, as well as emerging drug problems and technological developments, including online trade of drugs; - to support the civil society organisations by reinforcing their (i) advocacy function, (ii) capacity to make a difference at the local level, (iii) best practice sharing methods; - to support key stakeholders by expanding their knowledge and skills in the context of implementing minimum quality standards in drug demand reduction, particularly in the area of social integration; - to promote practical application of drug-related research, and, in particular, addiction research with a view of addressing current challenges and new threats. This call will fund activities on: - data collection, surveys and research activities; - training activities; - mutual learning, network development, identification and exchange of good practices, cooperation; - events, conferences, expert meetings; - dissemination and awareness-raising activities.","actionText":"[\"HOME Action Grant\"] [[{\"typeOfAction\":\"JUST-DRUGS-AG HOME Action Grant\",\"typeOfMGA\":[]}]]","budgetSource":[],"budgetMeaning":"Source budget field; not an award or guaranteed per-project amount","eligibilityText":"1. Eligible countries All EU Member States, with the exception of the United Kingdom and Denmark. Albania and Montenegro. 2. Eligibility and admissibility conditions: see section 5 of the call for proposals . 3. Indicative timetable for evaluation and grant agreement: see section 3 of the call for proposals . 4. Proposal templates and model grant agreements (MGA): Guide for applicants Standard proposal template M ulti-beneficiary Model Grant Agreement Members of consortium are required to conclude a consortium agreement, in principle prior to the signature of the grant agreement. 6. Additional documents: Annual Work Programme 2019 Justice Programme legal basis EU Financial Regulation","eligibilityVerified":false,"topicConditionsHtml":["<p><b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;&#xA;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;&#xA;color:#003366;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-bidi-language:&#xA;AR-SA\">1.&nbsp;&nbsp; Eligible countries</span></b></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;&#xA;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;&#xA;color:#003366;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-bidi-language:&#xA;AR-SA\">All EU&nbsp;Member States, with the exception of the United Kingdom and Denmark.<br />\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;&#xA;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;&#xA;color:#003366;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-bidi-language:&#xA;AR-SA\">Albania and Montenegro.</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;&#xA;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;&#xA;color