{"schemaVersion":1,"canonicalId":"eu-ft:topic:JUST-DRUGS-AG","identifier":"JUST-DRUGS-AG","sourceReference":"43365402HOMEActionGrant1606953600000","source":"EU Funding & Tenders Portal","sourceType":"1","mechanism":"grant","title":"Supporting initiatives in the Field of Drugs Policy","callIdentifier":"JUST-2020-AG-DRUGS","programmeCode":"31070247","programmePeriod":"2014 - 2020","status":"closed","sourceStatusCodes":["31094503"],"openings":["2020-12-03T00:00:00.000Z"],"deadlines":["2021-04-22T17:00:00.000Z"],"nextDeadline":null,"deadlineModel":"single-stage","description":"Scope : Project applications submitted under the present call for proposals must address at least one of the following priorities: - to support activities in the area of epidemiology of use of new psychoactive substances, including potent synthetic opioids, as well as emerging drug problems (notably on challenges related to cocaine and heroin use) and technological developments, including online trade of drugs; - to support the civil society organisations by reinforcing their (i) advocacy function, (ii) capacity to make a difference at the local level, (iii) best practice sharing methods; - to support key stakeholders by expanding their knowledge and skills in the context of implementing minimum quality standards in drug demand reduction (also on development of tools which would allow to measure possible improvements), particularly in the area of social integration and vulnerable groups; - to promote practical application of drug-related research, and, in particular, addiction research with a view of addressing current challenges and new threats. The following types of activities are eligible under this call for proposals: analytical activities, such as data collection, development of common methodologies, surveys, research activities, evaluations, workshops, experts meetings; training activities, such as staff exchanges, workshops, seminars, train-the-trainer events, online trainings; mutual learning, cooperation, awareness-raising and dissemination activities, such as identification and exchange of good practices, peer reviews, conferences, seminars, information campaigns, publications, ICT systems and tools; networking activities.","actionText":"[\"HOME Action Grant\"] [[{\"typeOfAction\":\"JUST-DRUGS-AG HOME Action Grant\",\"typeOfMGA\":[]}]]","budgetSource":[],"budgetMeaning":"Source budget field; not an award or guaranteed per-project amount","eligibilityText":"1. Eligible countries With the exception of international organisations, applicants and co-applicants must be established in the following countries to be eligible:  - The Member States of the European Union with the exception of Denmark (&ldquo;Member States participating in the Justice programme&rdquo;) - Albania and Montenegro - International organisations can be established outside the above-mentioned countries. For UK applicants: Please note that the United Kingdom is not bound by Regulation (EU) No 1382/2013 establishing the Justice programme and its implementing decisions and UK entities are therefore not eligible to participate under this call. 2. Eligibility and admissibility conditions: D escribed in section 4 of the Call document . 3. Selection criteria: Described in section 6 and 7 of the Call document . 4. Indicative timetable for evaluation and grant agreement: D escribed in section 3 of the Call document . 5. Proposal templates, evaluation forms and model agreements Guide for applicants Standard proposal template Multi-beneficiary Model Grant Agreement Members of consortium are required to conclude a consortium agreement, in principle prior to the signature of the grant agreement. 6. Additional documents: Annual Work Programme Justice Programme legal basis EU Financial Regulation","eligibilityVerified":false,"topicConditionsHtml":["<p><b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;&#10;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;&#10;color:#003366;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-bidi-language:&#10;AR-SA\">1.&nbsp;&nbsp; Eligible countries</span></b></p>\r\n<p>With the exception of international organisations, applicants and co-applicants must be established in the following countries to be eligible: </p>\r\n<p>- The Member States of the European Union with the exception of Denmark (&ldquo;Member States participating in the Justice programme&rdquo;)&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>- Albania and Montenegro</p>\r\n<p>- International organisations can be established outside the above-mentioned countries. <br />\r\n&nbsp;<br />\r\nFor UK applicants: Please note that the United Kingdom is not bound by Regulation (EU) No 1382/2013 establishing the Justice programme and its implementing decisions and UK entities are therefore not eligible to participate under this call.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;&#10;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;&#10;color:#003366;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-bidi-language:&#10;AR-SA\">2.&nbsp;&nbsp; Eligibility and admissibility conditions:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;&#10;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"> </span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB\">D<span style=\"color: black; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;; font-size: 9pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 115%; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;\">escribed in section 4 of the <a href=\"https://ec.europa.eu/research/participants/data/ref/other_eu_prog/justice/wp-call/call-fiche_just-2020-ag-drugs_en.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Call document</a>.<br />\r\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span><br />\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB\"> </span></p>\n<p><b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;&#10;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;&#10;color:#003366;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-bidi-language:&#10;AR-SA\">3.&nbsp;&nbsp; Selection criteria:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;&#10;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"> </span></p>\r\n<p>Described in section 6 and 7 of the <a href=\"https://ec.europa.eu/research/participants/data/ref/other_eu_prog/justice/wp-call/call-fiche_just-2020-ag-drugs_en.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Call document</a>.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;&#10;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;&#10;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;&#10;color:#003366;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-bidi-language:&#10;AR-SA\">4.&nbsp;&nbsp; Indicative timetable for evaluation and grant agreement:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;&#10;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"> </span></p>\r\n<p><font face=\"&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">D<span style=\"color: black; line-height: 115%; font-size: 9pt;\">escribed in section 3 of the <a href=\"https://ec.europa.eu/research/participants/data/ref/other_eu_prog/justice/wp-call/call-fiche_just-2020-ag-drugs_en.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Call document</a>.</span></font></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p><strong><font face=\"&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">5. Proposal templates, evaluation forms and model agreements</font></strong></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 51, 102); font-size: 9pt;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 51, 102); font-size: 9pt;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 51, 102); font-size: 9pt;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><a href=\"https://ec.europa.eu/research/participants/data/ref/other_eu_prog/common/justdrugs-isfp-isfb-amif_guide-applicants-20_en.pdf\" style=\"color: rgb(40, 151, 183); text-decoration: none;\" target=\"_blank\">Guide for applicants</a></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"background-color: rgb(198, 219, 239); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); display: inline; float: none; font-family: eui-light,Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size: 12.6px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;\"> </span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 51, 102); font-size: 9pt;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 51, 102); font-size: 9pt;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 51, 102); font-size: 9pt;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 51, 102); font-size: 9pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><a href=\"https://ec.europa.eu/research/participants/data/ref/other_eu_prog/common/tpl/pt/justdrugs-isfp-isfb-amif_call-pt-20_en.pdf\" style=\"color: rgb(40, 151, 183); text-decoration: none;\" target=\"_blank\">Standard proposal template</a></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 3px 0px; text-align: left; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-transform: none; line-height: 1.5; text-indent: 0px; letter-spacing: normal; font-family: eui-light,Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size: 12.6px; font-variant: normal; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: normal; orphans: 2; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\"><a href=\"https://ec.europa.eu/research/participants/data/ref/other_eu_prog/common/justdrugs-isfp-isfb-amif_mga-multi_en.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Multi-beneficiary Model Grant Agreement</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Members of consortium are required to conclude a consortium agreement, in principle prior to the signature of the grant agreement.</p>\n<p><b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;&#10;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;&#10;color:#003366;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-bidi-language:&#10;AR-SA\">6.&nbsp;&nbsp; Additional documents:<br />\r\n</span><